.TH INTRO 8
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to system administration
.SH DESCRIPTION
This section describes how the machine is built, started and checked:
the tools that turn source into a bootable image, what the kernel does
between the firmware handing it control and a shell prompt, and the
checks that run on every boot to say the machine is what it claims to be.
None of these pages describes a command typed at an
.IR rc (1)
prompt.
They describe the machine itself, from the outside.
.PP
The
.IR build (8)
driver compiles the kernel and the ring 3 programs, stages a bootable
disk, and starts it under QEMU.
.IR Boot (8)
describes what happens once the firmware gives control to the kernel:
the order things come up in, the disks, and the name space the first
program inherits.
.IR Init (8)
describes that first program, the shell script that starts the window
system and becomes the console's shell.
.IR Verify (8)
describes the self-tests that run on every boot, and how to read one
that fails.
.IR Lint (8)
checks the prose in comments and documents against a controlled
subset of English.
.IR Genfont (8)
regenerates the bitmap font the console and the toolkit share.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR build (8),
.IR boot (8),
.IR init (8),
